{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"verdict\": \"discrepancy\",\n  \"statementAssessment\": \"The claims that n+1>n, n+n=2n, n+n is even, and the sum of two even naturals is even are true. The inference that n+n being even implies n is even is false.\",\n  \"methodAssessment\": \"The described witness k=n correctly proves that n+n is even from n+n=2n. Adding witnesses for two even summands is also a valid method for proving their sum even. The rendered description supplies no proof of n+1>n or of the claim that n+n even implies n even.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"sourceAssertion\": \"“Since n+n is even, n is even.”\",\n      \"formalCounterpart\": \"No counterpart is described in the rendered formal argument.\",\n      \"classification\": \"false statement\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The implication does not hold for arbitrary natural n. For n=1, n+n=2 is even, while 1 is odd.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Take n=1: 1+1=2=2·1, but there is no natural k with 1=2k.\",\n      \"uncertainty\": \"None about the mathematical counterexample; the supplied text does not give exact formal theorem signatures.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"sourceAssertion\": \"“For a natural n, n+1>n.”\",\n      \"formalCounterpart\": \"No counterpart is described.\",\n      \"classification\": \"omission\",\n      \"explanation\": \"This source claim is true, but the rendered formal argument does not mention or establish it.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The described formal proof covers n+n=2n, evenness, and a final conditional statement.\",\n      \"uncertainty\": \"The audit is limited to the supplied description of the formal argument.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"sourceAssertion\": \"“Also n+n=2n. Consequently n+n is even.”\",\n      \"formalCounterpart\": \"The formal argument proves n+n=2n and then proves there exists k with n+n=2k by choosing k=n.\",\n      \"classification\": \"faithful correspondence\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The equality and the evenness conclusion correspond directly; k=n is the required witness.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Substituting k=n gives 2k=2n=n+n.\",\n      \"uncertainty\": \"None.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"sourceAssertion\": \"“Finally the sum of two even naturals is even.”\",\n      \"formalCounterpart\": \"The formal argument proves the last conditional statement by adding two explicit even-number witnesses.\",\n      \"classification\": \"faithful correspondence\",\n      \"explanation\": \"If the witnesses are a=2u and b=2v, then a+b=2(u+v), so the sum is even. This is a valid witness-based proof of the general claim.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Given witnesses u and v for the two even numbers, u+v witnesses evenness of their sum.\",\n      \"uncertainty\": \"The rendered description does not give the exact quantifiers, but the stated witness method is valid for the source claim.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"examinedAssertions\": [\n    {\n      \"assertion\": \"“For a natural n, n+1>n.”\",\n      \"assessment\": \"True, but omitted from the described formal argument.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Successor is strictly greater than its natural-number predecessor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"assertion\": \"“Also n+n=2n.”\",\n      \"assessment\": \"True and proved by the described formal argument.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The formal argument explicitly proves this equality.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"assertion\": \"“Consequently n+n is even.”\",\n      \"assessment\": \"True and supported by the described witness proof.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Choose k=n in n+n=2k.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"assertion\": \"“Since n+n is even, n is even.”\",\n      \"assessment\": \"False.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"For n=1, n+n=2 is even but n is odd.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"assertion\": \"“Finally the sum of two even naturals is even.”\",\n      \"assessment\": \"True; the described witness method proves it.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"If the summands are 2u and 2v, their sum is 2(u+v).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"omissions\": [\n    \"The formal argument description does not address n+1>n.\",\n    \"The formal argument description does not address the false implication from n+n even to n even.\"\n  ],\n  \"toolsUsed\": [\n    \"Read /input/INPUT.md with a shell command.\"\n  ],\n  \"checkingStatus\": \"Mathematical comparison of the supplied exposition and rendered formal argument only. No Lean checks were run; the input is not an original Lean module.\"\n}"}}
